<div class="doc-header">
  <h1>CIVORA — COMPLETE WEBSITE, CODEBASE &amp; FEATURE IMPLEMENTATION AUDIT</h1>
  <p><strong>Comprehensive Technical Architecture, Security, Workflow &amp; Readiness Evaluation</strong></p>
  <div class="metadata-grid">
    <div class="metadata-row">
      <div class="metadata-cell"><strong>Date:</strong> October 19, 2026</div>
      <div class="metadata-cell"><strong>Scope:</strong> Full Repository (client, server, prisma, tests)</div>
      <div class="metadata-cell"><strong>Audit Mode:</strong> Read-Only Verification</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metadata-row">
      <div class="metadata-cell"><strong>Lead Auditor:</strong> Principal Systems Architect</div>
      <div class="metadata-cell"><strong>Target Database:</strong> PostgreSQL (Cevora)</div>
      <div class="metadata-cell"><strong>Backend Tests:</strong> 241/241 Passing (100%)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>A comprehensive, systematic read-only technical audit of the Civora (Civic Issue Reporting &amp; Public Accountability) application was conducted across the entire codebase to evaluate its architectural integrity, implemented features, database schema, user roles, security, and readiness for future modules.</p>

<div class="callout-success">
  <strong>Key Architectural Finding:</strong> Modules 1 through 16 are genuinely implemented, integrated, and verified end-to-end. The platform features 21 active frontend routes and 17 backend API routers supported by 19 database models, 16 enums, and 9 database migrations. All 241 backend tests pass cleanly with zero failures.
</div>

<div class="callout-warning">
  <strong>Contractor Module Finding:</strong> The application visibly provides demo logins for Citizen, Official, and Admin only. Our audit confirmed that <strong>no usable contractor functionality currently exists</strong> in the application. While the foundation migration contains dormant schema entities (<code>Contractor</code>, <code>WorkOrder</code>, <code>ExecutionProgressUpdate</code>), there is <strong>no CONTRACTOR user role</strong>, no contractor registration or authentication, no contractor workspace, no tender/bidding models or workflows, and no milestone submission endpoints.
</div>

<h2>2. Verified Technology Stack &amp; Repository Structure</h2>
<p>The technology stack and versions were directly verified from <code>client/package.json</code> and <code>server/package.json</code>:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Layer</th>
      <th>Technology</th>
      <th>Verified Version</th>
      <th>Implementation Details</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Frontend Framework</strong></td>
      <td>React / React DOM</td>
      <td><code>^19.2.8</code></td>
      <td>Component architecture, Hooks, Context API. Cleanly bundled without hydration mismatches.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Build Tooling</strong></td>
      <td>Vite</td>
      <td><code>^8.3.0</code></td>
      <td>Production bundle: 890 KB JS (223 KB gzip), 107 KB CSS (20 KB gzip). Built in 661ms.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Styling</strong></td>
      <td>Tailwind CSS v4</td>
      <td><code>^4.3.3</code></td>
      <td><code>@tailwindcss/vite</code> with cohesive civic tokens (slate-950 canvas, civic blue, emerald).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Geospatial Map</strong></td>
      <td>Leaflet</td>
      <td><code>^1.9.4</code></td>
      <td>Interactive OpenStreetMap tile layer with ~110m privacy jitter and bounding box queries.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Linter</strong></td>
      <td>Oxlint</td>
      <td><code>^1.81.0</code></td>
      <td>Rust-based linter. 79 files inspected with <strong>0 errors</strong>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Backend Server</strong></td>
      <td>Node.js + Express</td>
      <td><code>^4.21.2</code></td>
      <td>Modular Express architecture with CORS, JSON body parser, and centralized error handler.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Database &amp; ORM</strong></td>
      <td>PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM</td>
      <td><code>^6.19.3</code></td>
      <td>19 tables, 16 enums, 58 indexes. Exact <code>Decimal(14,2)</code> precision for financial fields.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Authentication</strong></td>
      <td>JWT + Bcrypt</td>
      <td><code>^9.0.3</code> / <code>^3.0.3</code></td>
      <td>Dual transport: HttpOnly SameSite cookie (<code>civora_auth_token</code>) + Bearer header fallback.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Validation</strong></td>
      <td>Zod</td>
      <td><code>^4.6.7</code></td>
      <td>Strict schema validation on all incoming request bodies, queries, and route params.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>File Uploads</strong></td>
      <td>Multer</td>
      <td><code>^2.4.0</code></td>
      <td>Memory storage with SHA-256 checksums, magic-byte inspection, and disk storage in <code>uploads/</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Security</strong></td>
      <td>Rate Limiters</td>
      <td><code>^8.7.1</code></td>
      <td>Layered limits on complaint submission, comments, public tracking, and authentication.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

