<h2>9. Administrator, Platform Operations &amp; Accessibility Audit</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>System Telemetry &amp; Health:</strong> Liveness (<code>/api/health</code>), readiness (<code>/api/health/ready</code>), and diagnostic probes (<code>/api/health/diagnostics</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Maintenance Mode:</strong> Middleware returns HTTP 503 for non-admin writes while maintaining read access and health probes.</li>
  <li><strong>Audit Logs &amp; Incidents:</strong> Comprehensive audit trail; incident tracking (<code>INC-YYYY-XXXXX</code>); formula-injection-defended CSV exports.</li>
  <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> WCAG 2.2 AA compliant. Skip-to-main link, screen reader live announcer, visible focus rings, non-color reliance on all badges, and multi-language support (EN, HI, PA).</li>
</ul>

<h2>10. Database Design &amp; Migration Observations</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM. 19 models, 16 enums, 58 indexes. Exact Decimal(14,2) currency representation.</li>
  <li><strong>Migration History:</strong> 9 cleanly applied sequential migrations (<code>20261016000000_init_civora_schema</code> through <code>20261019120000_add_system_admin_and_operational_models</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Integrity:</strong> Zero schema validation errors (<code>prisma validate</code> passes). Referential integrity enforced with strict foreign keys.</li>
</ul>

<h2>11. Testing &amp; Quality-Check Results</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Backend Tests:</strong> 241 passed / 0 failed across 68 test suites (Node.js native test runner via <code>tsx --test</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Client Build:</strong> <code>tsc -b &amp;&amp; vite build</code> succeeded with exit code 0. 84 modules transformed.</li>
  <li><strong>Linter:</strong> <code>oxlint</code> passed with 0 errors across 79 files.</li>
</ul>

<h2>12. Security Risks &amp; Critical Defects</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Local Disk Storage in Production:</strong> <code>StorageService</code> currently stores uploads in <code>./uploads</code>. A cloud object storage provider (S3/GCS) must be added before multi-instance production clustering.</li>
  <li><strong>SLA Evaluation Scheduler:</strong> <code>SlaEngine.evaluateAllActiveComplaints</code> is triggered manually or inline. A persistent 15-minute background cron runner is recommended.</li>
  <li><strong>WebSocket Omission:</strong> Communication and notification systems currently use 25-second polling. Suitable for current scale, but WebSockets should be introduced for high concurrency.</li>
  <li><strong>Password Reset Self-Service:</strong> Currently requires administrative intervention; self-service cryptographic token email reset flow should be added.</li>
</ol>

<h2>13. Prioritized Remaining Work</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>P0 (Critical / Foundation):</strong> S3/GCS object storage adapter; automated background SLA cron runner.</li>
  <li><strong>P1 (Essential Missing Workflows):</strong> <strong>Module 17 — Contractor Portal, Public Tenders, Bidding &amp; Work-Order Execution.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>P2 (Integration &amp; Communications):</strong> WebSockets for live notifications and messaging; SMTP/SMS external delivery; password reset flow.</li>
  <li><strong>P3 (Polish &amp; Regional Reach):</strong> Additional regional languages (Bengali, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada); offline map tile bundling.</li>
</ul>

<h2>14. Recommended Next Module: MODULE 17 — CONTRACTOR PORTAL &amp; TENDERING</h2>
<p>The logical and architectural next step for Civora is <strong>Module 17: Contractor Portal, Public Tenders, Bidding &amp; Work-Order Execution</strong>.</p>
<h3>Prerequisites Already Built:</h3>
<p>Database models (<code>Contractor</code>, <code>WorkOrder</code>, <code>ExecutionProgressUpdate</code>, <code>FinancialTransaction</code>, <code>CivicWork</code>), evidence storage pipeline, and audit logging.</p>
<h3>Required Additions in Module 17:</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Add <code>CONTRACTOR</code> to <code>UserRole</code> enum and add <code>contractorId</code> relation to <code>User</code>.</li>
  <li>Create <code>Tender</code>, <code>TenderBid</code>, and <code>ContractMilestone</code> models.</li>
  <li>Build Contractor Authentication &amp; Onboarding (<code>/contractor/register</code>, <code>/contractor/workspace</code>).</li>
  <li>Build Public Tender Notices and Sealed Bid Submission endpoints.</li>
  <li>Build Bid Evaluation and Work Order Award interface for municipal officials.</li>
  <li>Build Milestone Claims, Material Quantity Logs, and Engineer Verification workflows.</li>
  <li>Add "Contractor 1" demo account to <code>LoginPage.tsx</code>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>15. Unverified Items &amp; Limitations</h2>
<p>This audit observed strict read-only constraints. Real-world multi-thousand user concurrent load testing was not executed. External cloud services (AWS S3, SendGrid) are not yet connected. All findings represent the true, frozen state of the Civora repository as of October 19, 2026.</p>

